(begin-tx "TX-S1-02 - RETIRED: the migration it tested no longer exists")
(print "")
(print "=== TX-S1-02 — RETIRED 2026-11-10 ====================================================")
(print "")
(print "THIS BLOCK TESTED `RPS.UM_FVT|BackfillS1Counters`, the ONE-SHOT S1 counter migration.")
(print "It ran on mainnet on 2026-11-10 against all nine FVTs and was then DELETED from the")
(print "module: a migration that has executed is dead surface, and Pact can never remove a")
(print "definition from a deployed module -- only a redeploy without it can. So the function is")
(print "gone, and a test of a function that does not exist cannot be kept.")
(print "")
(print "WHAT IT MEASURED, recorded here because the numbers are the evidence the round worked:")
(print "  earning-leg-count, per FVT:  Bloodshed 9 · CodingDivision 15 · CompanyShares 7")
(print "                               Nosferatu 13 · OuroLpFarm 25 · Snakes 7 · Stoicism 4")
(print "                               Subsidiary 59 · WonderCoach 13")
(print "  dormant, per lane:           Stoicism/WSTOA 0 · Subsidiary/AURYN 2 · OuroLpFarm/OURO 0")
(print "Every one matched the figure predicted from live state before the transaction was sent.")
(print "")
(print "WHAT IS STILL COVERED, and by what:")
(print "  the counters' ONGOING maintenance  -> TX-S1-01 (descent to 1, the lane sweeps to 0.0)")
(print "  the DORMANT branch                 -> TX-S1-03 (zero-stake last claimant sweeps)")
(print "  the absent-COLUMN semantics        -> TX-S1-COL (and _newcolumnsafety.py)")
(print "  the restore's zero-refusal         -> TX-S1-COL")
(print "Nothing that survives the migration lost its test; only the migration's own did.")
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
